{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": "Dig & Discover tuning (GDD §17: everything configurable). Distances in world units (1 block = 1 unit). materials: durability = hit points, minPower = weakest tool power that can dig it, value = sell price per item, drops = items per block; block = the KayKit block model drawn for it, pickup = what flies into the backpack, decor = pieces poking out of the top (nuggets on ores, gems on crystals) so they read from above. zones: rings around the hub by distance (from = where the zone starts; edges are wobbly); fill = the zone's base rock (its minPower gates the zone behind a tool tier), patches/ores = {id, chance} mixed in. finds: the artifacts to collect (GDD §11) — 3 per zone (`zone`, 0-based), each buried exactly once at a seeded spot in its zone and revealed when a tunnel reaches it, worth `reward` cash; `rarity` drives the find banner. The collection totem in the hub shows found vs missing; finding them all completes the collection (`collectionReward`). wardrobe: looks bought with cash at the hub closet (colors, faces under images/non-preload/skins, hats under models/hats; hat placement in ui/hatfits.json). tools: the upgrade path shown as a timeline at the ATM (`rarity` colours a tool once owned, grey until then), ending with the tractor (`vehicle`: ridden in the mine, see `tractor`). tractor: the look of the last tool; the miner rides it outside the hub (smoke puff on the way out and back in): height = tractor height in world units, rotationY turns the model (radians), seat = where the miner sits (tractor-local, world units), speedMultiplier on walking speed, smoke = the puff, exhaust = small puffs while driving (tractor-local position, seconds between puffs). Edited in the level editor Tractor tab. achievements: claimed at the HUD trophy button; stat = blocks (dug) / ores (ore blocks dug) / earned (cash from selling and finds) / finds (artifacts collected); each tier pays its reward when claimed, and claiming the last unlocks its decor (named here, placed in levels/hub.json achievementDecor). firstFindAfterBlocks: the first artifact turns up on this many blocks dug (wherever the miner digs), so every new player finds one early; its buried copy is removed.",
